; TREE BRUSH: fir on its side (tip right), strokes from the centre line out to the edge,
; thick to thin, painted tip -> base. 75 strokes.
; row order (0 = tip; some rows skipped and painted two rows later): [0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 8, 9, 7, 10, 11, 12, 14, 15, 13, 16, 18, 19, 17, 20, 21, 23, 24, 22, 25, 26, 27, 28, 30, 31, 29, 33, 34, 32, 35, 36, 37]
; offsets from data/calibration.json: X -14.5  Y +7.1  Z +1.1
; BEFORE STARTING: cartridge OFF (G28 raises the bed to nozzle height). Card in the frame.
; Load the brush with paint by hand at the pause (no jar dipping in this file).
M104 S0
M140 S0
M107
G21
G90
G28 ; home with the cartridge off
G1 Z65.10 F600 ; bed down for attaching the brush
M400
M117 Attach loaded brush, Resume
@pause ; snap the cartridge on (brush loaded with paint), then press Resume
G1 Z26.10 F600 ; stay well clear of the paper and frame
